{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547448-trench-crusade-meets-world-of-darkness","id":1547448,"title":"Trench Crusade Meets World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-02T02:07:54-08:00","id":1547448,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Trench Crusade Meets World of Darkness","content":"So Imagine the following scenario. The history of Wod goes more or less how it goes in canon, vampires skulking in the shadows, werewolves guarding they forests and mages studying reality. Until the First Crusade where the Knights Templar found <i>Something </i>in Jerusalem that drove them to throw open the gates to hell in an act simply known as the first Heresy and user in a new era of madness and death as the demons run rampant in Europe and in response rally the forces of the faithful on a crusade to retake Jerusalem and kick the demons back into hell. The crusade current year is 1914 AD, Marking the 900th year of this Crusade.<br /> <br /> Now Most of Central Europe are reduced into a mess of mud and trenches as the Faithful and Heretic fight for inches of land. Infernal engines of war spew forth from ruined Jerusalem to do battle with they equivalents from blessed war factories of New Antioch and the many Homunculi grown by the alchemists of the Iron Sultanate and processions of armed Pilgrims still march toward the infernal ruins of Jerusalem still intent on reclaiming it from the forces of Hell.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Trench Crusade:<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://mediaproxy.tvtropes.org/width/1200/https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/345624663_248288767682979_1721314797394324424_n_0.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://mediaproxy.tvtropes.org/width/1200/https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/345624663_248288767682979_1721314797394324424_n_0.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://mediaproxy.tvtropes.org/width/1200/https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/345624663_248288767682979_1721314797394324424_n_0.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> And all the WOD splats caught Right in the middle of this mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T08:25:06-08:00","id":1547458,"title":"","content":"I suspect that from the perspective of the Umbra-going games, that would make most of the affected lands akin to Broken Mirrors (no gauntlet in the worst ways possible).<br /> <br /> In any case, a nine century war sounds like a way to keep the Garou out of other trouble for a very, very long time. This could even be like a reverse Amazon War for the Garou Nation, where Fera come around to help them and take their territory to get it done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T11:47:29-08:00","id":1547460,"title":"","content":"This would... take a lot more work than I think you're considering. The Trench Crusade's setup is functional for a small war-game that just needs enough window dressing to create a unique atmosphere to pull in some mini warriors from other games they're getting tired of. Most wargames never build up the following for deep lore exploration like Battletech of WH40K do, so they don't worry about how fast and loose they're playing with things.<br /> <br /> RPGs have to be more invested in functional lore because the focus on playing individual characters means you need to understand an AU well enough to actually play someone living in it. Wargames can get away with tossing around words like &quot;blessed&quot; or &quot;infernal,&quot; to just handwave the logistical nonsense of a 900 year war at this sort of scale. In our real history, &quot;The Crusades&quot; in most people's minds are really just the first three ones that actually involved Christian military expeditions into the Middle East. They were immensely draining on Europe in pretty every imaginable way, and the rest of the Crusades were largely fought in Europe to either fend off powers trying to capitalize on that, persecute religious minorities (both non-Christian and Christian alike), or just Church sanctioned wars between Christian kingdoms as kings tried to rob each other to recover the former wealth of their nations. <br /> <br /> In a RPG, a 900 year war is either powered by forces some immense the PCs are likely unable to engage with them in a meaningful fashion (and thus vastly limit players that want to do things like end the war by doing daring raids on vital enemy strategic points), or is going to be so grimdark the Garou would all be dead of Harano a few centuries ago.<br /> <br /> And all of that is before we even try to get to melding these to settings which is... a bigger ask than I think it sounds like on the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T11:52:27-08:00","id":1547462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547448-trench-crusade-meets-world-of-darkness?p=1547458#post1547458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that from the perspective of the Umbra-going games, that would make most of the affected lands akin to Broken Mirrors (no gauntlet in the worst ways possible).<br /> <br /> In any case, a nine century war sounds like a way to keep the Garou out of other trouble for a very, very long time. This could even be like a reverse Amazon War for the Garou Nation, where Fera come around to help them and take their territory to get it done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that and due to lack of a colonial age thanks to the fact Europe is distracted by a demonic invasion means two fera genocides are butterfly away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T17:31:43-08:00","id":1548077,"title":"","content":"To repost my comment on this idea from spacebattles,<br /> <br /> the Mummies are mostly unaware due to them being asleep, but the ones who are active likely are very against the demons and make their displeasure very well known. They probably also want to study the miracles of the mortals.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge probably are extinct due to purges against the infernal sadly, and the MM probably is publicly operating with papal approval.<br /> <br /> The Lancea likely are firmly against the demons if for no other reason than the Lancea think they as vampires are still serving God. The Invictus likely doesn't want to bow to any demon lord, the Dracul might go either way, and the carthians likely are against both.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters would be a pain in the ass to deal with and their powers would make them great at fighting the infernal, either from raising the dead, saving souls and coming back from death, or from their habit of making cults to help ghosts and mortals alike. Though they'd likely take abrhamic roots so they aren't killed by the mortals for heresy. Also, given how ww1 resulted in modern sin-eater society from how many sin-eaters popped up, the war of Trench crusade would have made the Sin-Eaters the dominant splat in terms of numbers.<br /> <br /> Werewolves likely are the same, they will be fighting on the front because they love to fight but just as many will be holding their own territory. I'm sure some will change their beliefs to make it so Luna is...idk the wife of Christ, or father wolf was an angel or something. Luna should be helping and may have called a silver crusade and sent the lunes to help. The Firstborn will be active as well and will be monstrous for the demons to deal with given how they are lesser gods.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters would vary krewe to krewe but I see them operating as small units to take out demons or help the dead. The mages will be pushed hard by all sides, they'd probably be happiest in the Islamic world due to their more accepting view on alchemy and magic shit. The mummies vary to much for a single front or method. Though any who wake up in demon territory likely make that territory barren and lifeless. Beasts idk. Prometheans likely vary but are probably more focused on their own paths and pilgramages.<br /> <br /> The mages I can't see forming the seers of the throne or the modern Pentacle. Given how the demons aren't agents of the Exarchs there may even be an alliance since neither group wants the world dead or run by the devils.\u200b<br /> <br /> The Ordo I feel would be split between demon worshippers/experimenters and those who decided they can do more experimentation with mortals than demons. They likely would go for mass embrace and freakish monsters to fight against their foes. The Cartians would prefer guriella warfare and propaganda along with exploiting the law. Invictius would likely go with the classical route of vampire warfare. The Lancea probably would align themselves hard with the church. I could see the Lancea acting as secret police for the church, watching for any who will succumb to sin, or being wolves pushing the masses forward in the trenches and defending pilgrims.<br /> <br /> The Khaibit likely have been put into overdrive in their duties of fighting the things in the dark. I'd imagine the strix would work with the demons.\u200b<br /> <br /> The Ahl al-Jabal are almost certainly active behind the wall and purging any supernatural they find. The Thule society is probably active in the HRE. The Aegis is probably still being the Aegis. Though given how they have the head of John the Baptist that is still telling prophecies the Church may have raided them. The Ascending ones likely are at the frontlines of battle and R&amp;D for their alchemy with how devout many of them are. Asclepeion likely have re-modeled to present themselves as blessed healers of Christ.<br /> <br /> Cheiron is certainly selling for all sides and their patrons likely are loving the money for weapon dealing.<br /> <br /> The Knight's of saint george likely were purged due to their alligence to abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> The rest likely are re-organized and have to adapt to a war footing and dealing with how susipious their neighbors will be of them.\u200b<br /> <br /> For WOD, The Sabbat hate infernalists more than about anything and would be firmly against the demons. I love the Tzimisce but they probably end up purged by the Church due to their connection with an Earthbound. The Salubri might end up ascendant or purged even harder, depends if Saulot decides against being eaten when Jerusalem explodes or if the castes unite in the holy land. If they do they probably follow the dav20 alt timeline where they join the Sabbat and murder infernalists everywhere.<br /> <br /> The Cam is going to struggle denying Caine and the ante's when hell is outside their door.<br /> <br /> The surviving setites are likely fully against the infernal and while doing their temptation thing they are very much against letting the world being the slave of demons.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim likely are operating semi-openly with the assassins and as judges of the vampires in the middle east.<br /> <br /> The Baali are two camps. One is having the time of their life. The Order of Moloch is having a panic attack.<br /> <br /> The technocracy is still forming in the timeline but they are probably the most dangerous weapon humanity has against the demons. No nukes yet but getting there. The traditions idk.<br /> <br /> The garou probably are causing several problems for themselves.<br /> <br /> the wraiths are miserable probably.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T09:42:10-08:00","id":1548111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547448-trench-crusade-meets-world-of-darkness?p=1548077#post1548077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For WOD, The Sabbat hate infernalists more than about anything and would be firmly against the demons. I love the Tzimisce but they probably end up purged by the Church due to their connection with an Earthbound. The Salubri might end up ascendant or purged even harder, depends if Saulot decides against being eaten when Jerusalem explodes or if the castes unite in the holy land. If they do they probably follow the dav20 alt timeline where they join the Sabbat and murder infernalists everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this divergence happened nine centuries ago, the modern constructions of Kindred society will not exist as they are in the normal game. That reaches back to before the Masquerade... which is either something they just wouldn't bother with if demons were literally pouring through, or would be really easy to use to just step back from everyone's attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Cam is going to struggle denying Caine and the ante's when hell is outside their door.<br /> <br /> The surviving setites are likely fully against the infernal and while doing their temptation thing they are very much against letting the world being the slave of demons.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim likely are operating semi-openly with the assassins and as judges of the vampires in the middle east.<br /> <br /> The Baali are two camps. One is having the time of their life. The Order of Moloch is having a panic attack. </div> </div> </div>Well, demonologists could be, up until they get in a struggle between factions that want them dead. The Silent Striders are also probably going to make sure that the numbers and movements of Setites are very well tracked, since if Sutekh has a million haters, they're among them. If Sutekh has only a thousand haters, it's the tribe alone. If he has just one hater, the tribe has taken massive hits, and if he has no haters, the tribe is dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The technocracy is still forming in the timeline but they are probably the most dangerous weapon humanity has against the demons. No nukes yet but getting there. The traditions idk. </div> </div> </div>Unlikely to exist as it is past the divergence. Mistridge happened in the 13th century, well after the divergence of Trench Crusade, so the Craftmasons would probably have aimed their guns at the demons and if anything like the Traditions vs Technocracy exists, it's probably as more of a rivalry or competition for who's the best demon killer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The garou probably are causing several problems for themselves. </div> </div> </div>Again, not with a nine century war. Someone else is going to have to take their place as &quot;tragically doomed maybe&quot;, because the number of mistakes that their more human-sympathizing numbers cause following along with European societal trends in the past millennium or so is no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the wraiths are miserable probably. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not. Perhaps they shuffle through and fight with purpose in the places where the spirit and material touch. It'd be kind of like being a Doomslayer, but closer to home and on much less treacherous ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T20:28:52-08:00","id":1548393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547448-trench-crusade-meets-world-of-darkness?p=1548111#post1548111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlikely to exist as it is past the divergence. Mistridge happened in the 13th century, well after the divergence of Trench Crusade, so the Craftmasons would probably have aimed their guns at the demons and if anything like the Traditions vs Technocracy exists, it's probably as more of a rivalry or competition for who's the best demon killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if any faction is going to become the technocracy equivalent then it's likely going to be a militarized version Cabal of Pure Thought and funnily enough they have might rough analogs of three technocratic Conventions if we go by TC lore.<br /> <br /> Those being the.mentalist order (in charge of mutating people into deformed mute giants called communicants which is right out of the 1sts ed progenitors's play book), the synod of strategic prophesy (rough analog of the NWO in the sense they're the intelligence arm of technocracy equivalent only intead of technology they use omens and vision from what they believe to be god) and whoever is in charge of the church space program (obversoly the void engineers equivalent.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547448-trench-crusade-meets-world-of-darkness?p=1548111#post1548111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not with a nine century war. Someone else is going to have to take their place as &quot;tragically doomed maybe&quot;, because the number of mistakes that their more human-sympathizing numbers cause following along with European societal trends in the past millennium or so is no longer a thing.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Yeah trench crusades Word of God has said multiple times that the colonial age isnt't a thing due to the forever war with hell it's self keeping everybody busy so it's likely that the extinction of both Camazotz and Bunayp is butterflied away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}